Issues to fix:
1. Backstop: `before_provider_request` fires for EVERY provider request, including the ones the gate would have parked... but aborting the session is drastic if it fires spuriously. Consider: during a window, main loop parks → no request. Non-parked requests: title-gen/side/advisors. Aborting the *session* for those is the strongest refusal. But there's a subtle danger: abort could fire for a request whose model is not DeepSeek! The gate pauses ALL LLM calls regardless of model (user asked "pause all llm calls"). Hmm — but should the pause apply only to DeepSeek-scheduled models? The user said "pause all llm calls ... due to deepseek peak pricing". Ambiguous. Pausing everything is the literal ask ("all llm calls"), and it's the conservative choice for cost. Also the gate can't distinguish models cheaply (payload has model info — `event.payload` contains the model? Possibly). Keep it simple: pause all, as asked. Document that it pauses everything including non-DeepSeek models, and windows are configurable.

Hmm, but that means during 01:00–10:00 UTC Mon–Fri the user's session is frozen even if they switch to Claude. Their instruction: "pause all llm calls". Fine — literal. I'll note it in the reply (and the config allows narrowing by disabling — or they could... hmm, can't filter by model currently). Should I add model filtering? Extra scope; skip, but mention.

2. `statusText` uses `new Date(next).toISOString().slice(11,16)` — ok.

3. `arm` is defined after `apply` uses `context` — fine.

4. Timer leak: `arm` may be called multiple times (session_start per session, /peak-gate reload) → clears previous. OK.

5. `heartbeat` every 30s calls apply with reason "heartbeat" → sends notify if `want && holding && cooldown`; cooldown 60s → during peak it'd notify every 60s! Bad: repeated notifications. Fix: only notify on transitions (engage) — i.e., notify only when engagement state changes from not-holding to holding. Use a `wasHolding`/`lastApplied` variable: notify when we transition open→engaged, and engaged→open.

Let me restructure apply:
```ts
const apply = (now, reason) => {
  const want = shouldPause(now);
  const wasHolding = holding;
  if (want && !agentPauseGate.paused) holding = agentPauseGate.pause();
  else if (!want && holding && agentPauseGate.paused) { agentPauseGate.resume(); holding = false; }
  else if (!want) holding = false;
  context?.ui.setStatus(...);
  if (holding && !wasHolding) notify(paused...)
  else if (!holding && wasHolding) notify(resumed)
};
```
And drop the cooldown/notify-timer complexity except the backstop's own throttle. Cleaner and no spam.

Also for the `startup` reason at session start during peak: notify once → good.

6. `reason` param: keep for messages? With transition-based notifications, `reason` is only used to suppress notifications on `command`. Simplify: notify on state change always (including command: e.g. `/peak-gate pause` → sets manual then apply → transition → notify "paused"; that's fine, plus the explicit notify in the command). Remove the double notify: let apply() handle it and commands not notify separately (or keep command-specific text). Simplify: commands call apply and rely on transition notify; `reload`/status print their own info. Let me restructure: apply(now) with transition notifications; drop "reason"; commands just call apply(now).

Actually keep a small distinction: on `resume`/`pause` commands notify explicit text; that duplicates the transition notify. Use only transition notify + command-specific lines for status/reload.

7. `manual` clearing on edge: `if (windows.length > 0) manual = undefined;` — hmm, if windows is empty (disabled) the edge timer reschedules every HEARTBEAT? With windows empty, nextTransition → undefined → delay = HEARTBEAT_MS, and manual never clears. Edge case: with empty windows the gate is off anyway. Simplify: always clear manual at an edge (real edge = windows exist). I'll clear manual whenever a real transition occurred: if `next !== undefined`. Implement via schedule(): capture whether next exists.

Let me rewrite the factory body cleanly in one edit (lines 179-246ish) to keep it readable.

Also: `let { windows, enabled, source } = loadWindows();` — `let` destructuring with reassignment of individual props requires `let` per var; destructuring with let is fine (windows/enabled/source mutable). ✓.

8. Backstop `ctx.abort()`: also, `before_provider_request` handler returning undefined → payload unchanged. ✓ 

One risk: `ctx.abort()` inside the hook triggers `options.signal.throwIfAborted()` in the boundary → the stream throws a DOMException. Does the *agent loop* handle that gracefully (turn aborted, no retry)? The abort path is the same as Ctrl+C → graceful. Also, title generation (not gated) — aborts session? ctx.abort() aborts the session's agent; title generation uses its own controller (#titleGenerationAbortController) — session.abort() aborts that too (line 8365). Good.

